From eb2d416da3c09d4858a1ea0403e94c9c920d994b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:44:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] r0dump: converge capture pipeline (early standard
 snapshot + nearby)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Keep the early standard_snapshot and the default-off synchronous
nearby_candidate experiment (bit 40, one attempt per DexFile identity),
routing all dump sites through the single capture pipeline. Remove the
constructor Header/RuntimeView snapshot and logical-data table overlay
that had no host consumption closure (§0.2 convergence), restoring the
original logical-data copy. Update capture/file/config tests and the
f2/f3/f4/f9 source contracts to match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I183be7711abf543193c42785ba5417f630371f1d
